# 1024: make the `.rc` oracle compile each cell with the options its manifest
#       entry carries (measurement-tool caliber fix; no compiler change).
#
# Why: `tools/raisa_oracle.py` used one hard-coded `-cc1 -triple ... -O2`
# command line for *every* cell, ignoring `case["options"]` in
# `docx/tests/llvm/tx8_blackbox/round2/manifest.json`.  Eight cells are not
# meant to be built that way (`-fraisa-short-ptr`: alloc_l1_short_ptr,
# mem_l1_multi_short_ptr; `-mllvm -riscv-bank-aware=true`: the four
# `*_bank_on` cells, mem_l1_multi_bank_on), so the oracle compared a
# configuration the vendor never ran.
#
# Measured effect of the fix (same binary, sweep 0/0):
#   alloc_l1_short_ptr      asm:DIFF obj:IDENTICAL -> asm:IDENTICAL obj:IDENTICAL
#   alloc_l1shared_bank_on  asm:DIFF obj:IDENTICAL -> asm:IDENTICAL obj:IDENTICAL
#   alloc_l0{a,w}shared_bank_on obj:IDENTICAL -> obj:DIFF (the bank layout really
#       is different once the pass runs; that is the `bank-aware-shared` item)
#   cell-level baseline: 94/103 -> 96/103 byte-identical, slots 195/11 unchanged.
#
# The options are filtered like `tools/corpus_parity.py::command()`: only
# `-mllvm -print-*` / `-debug-*` / diagnostic flags are dropped, everything
# else is appended to the cc1 command line for both sides and for every flavour
# (asm, obj, mir, --probe).
#
# Apply from the *tree root* (`cd wt-merge-e && patch -p1 < this.patch`); this
# is a tools/ patch, unlike the src/ compiler patches.
#
--- a/tools/raisa_oracle.py
+++ b/tools/raisa_oracle.py
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
